71	In the following sections, we will describe the Transformer, motivate\nself-attention and discuss its advantages over models such as [14, 15] and [8].\n3\nModel Architecture\nMost competitive neural sequence transduction models have an encoder-decoder structure [5, 2, 29].\nHere, the encoder maps an input sequence of symbol representations (x1, ..., xn) to a sequence\nof continuous representations z = (z1, ..., zn). Given z, the decoder then generates an output\nsequence (y1, ..., ym) of symbols one element at a time. At each step the model is auto-regressive\n[9], consuming the previously generated symbols as additional input when generating the next.	{"type": "text", "page": 2, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"6cd702d3-d017-4211-92e0-b88831febff7\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 2, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"4d24bbb8-00e7-4b4c-8d00-dc40397bb36c\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 2, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"9892f84627649c6514155be2968a73a9424688b491e8e96125b2d9937fb137b0\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"053eda32-f79b-4f20-8d5f-cb9dd0b99e28\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 2, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"5a47399525ed9c415b3e65d9c55cfc3d45fec547ed335f8193cab94764220da2\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"26e814a5-bbe7-4ee5-8014-46b8c976f5db\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"2b59210496000ea52ce47fedd9e0750f8d269e1f2fab8a7ae5373cd0203d54c4\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\"{key}: {value}\\", \\"metadata_separator\\": \\"\\\\n\\", \\"text\\": \\"\\", \\"mimetype\\": \\