76	Scaled Dot-Product Attention\nMulti-Head Attention\nFigure 2: (left) Scaled Dot-Product Attention. (right) Multi-Head Attention consists of several\nattention layers running in parallel.\nquery with all keys, divide each by √dk, and apply a softmax function to obtain the weights on the\nvalues.\nIn practice, we compute the attention function on a set of queries simultaneously, packed together\ninto a matrix Q. The keys and values are also packed together into matrices K and V . We compute\nthe matrix of outputs as:\nAttention(Q, K, V ) = softmax(QKT\n√dk\n)V\n(1)\nThe two most commonly used attention functions are additive attention [2], and dot-product (multi-\nplicative) attention. Dot-product attention is identical to our algorithm, except for the scaling factor\nof\n1\n√dk .	{"type": "text", "page": 4, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"f34fc98b-c34d-4052-91fa-f4f9c57c673f\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"7c46c85f-3fc4-4f09-a074-16b4c08d4469\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"4b78a1f2cfcc4dffd47567d88073d7b400eaeaa119a824bea0f8a3e5aa8eacfe\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"eaca8ccd-f3dd-4355-a62f-dcd1a154711f\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"95837db734e8c5870ab5eacca4b285c603dc5a2cd30b85ec4393e24b915a2d35\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\"{key}: {value}\\", \\"metadata_separator\\": \\"\\\\n\\", \\"text\\": \\"\\", \\"mimetype\\": \\"text/plain\\", \\"start_char_idx\\": 0, \\"end_char_idx\\": 772, \\"text_template\\": \\"{metadata_str}\\\\n\\\\n{content}\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"TextNode\\"}", "_node_type": "TextN