77	Dot-product attention is identical to our algorithm, except for the scaling factor\nof\n1\n√dk . Additive attention computes the compatibility function using a feed-forward network with\na single hidden layer. While the two are similar in theoretical complexity, dot-product attention is\nmuch faster and more space-efﬁcient in practice, since it can be implemented using highly optimized\nmatrix multiplication code.\nWhile for small values of dk the two mechanisms perform similarly, additive attention outperforms\ndot product attention without scaling for larger values of dk [3]. We suspect that for large values of\ndk, the dot products grow large in magnitude, pushing the softmax function into regions where it has\nextremely small gradients 4. To counteract this effect, we scale the dot products by\n1\n√dk .	{"type": "text", "page": 4, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"eaca8ccd-f3dd-4355-a62f-dcd1a154711f\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"7c46c85f-3fc4-4f09-a074-16b4c08d4469\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"4b78a1f2cfcc4dffd47567d88073d7b400eaeaa119a824bea0f8a3e5aa8eacfe\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"f34fc98b-c34d-4052-91fa-f4f9c57c673f\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"e80cbc5ee3ecf93ab76eb02c52e7b3fcdfb0dacfaee596959659fe9775b422c4\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"ba36e7f4-0679-47d8-acfd-77136217314a\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"f27d02f1d91aded7e3f4e9799279b000257e41f1598699ad5b61bb36278631c2\\", \\"class_