78	To counteract this effect, we scale the dot products by\n1\n√dk .\n3.2.2\nMulti-Head Attention\nInstead of performing a single attention function with dmodel-dimensional keys, values and queries,\nwe found it beneﬁcial to linearly project the queries, keys and values h times with different, learned\nlinear projections to dk, dk and dv dimensions, respectively. On each of these projected versions of\nqueries, keys and values we then perform the attention function in parallel, yielding dv-dimensional\noutput values. These are concatenated and once again projected, resulting in the ﬁnal values, as\ndepicted in Figure 2.\nMulti-head attention allows the model to jointly attend to information from different representation\nsubspaces at different positions. With a single attention head, averaging inhibits this.	{"type": "text", "page": 4, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"ba36e7f4-0679-47d8-acfd-77136217314a\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"7c46c85f-3fc4-4f09-a074-16b4c08d4469\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"4b78a1f2cfcc4dffd47567d88073d7b400eaeaa119a824bea0f8a3e5aa8eacfe\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"eaca8ccd-f3dd-4355-a62f-dcd1a154711f\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 4, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"f289eacf98d804d252908ff1fdb33d65a9eac0d8f2c283f99552608d5215596e\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"36943a66-d21e-482c-a192-1c9ba0027660\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"04b85a089c3c2d8eba46a2caa72f48579d421080f44b7656c7f8ee83c64ffa19\\", \\"class_na