83	This\nconsists of two linear transformations with a ReLU activation in between.\nFFN(x) = max(0, xW1 + b1)W2 + b2\n(2)\nWhile the linear transformations are the same across different positions, they use different parameters\nfrom layer to layer. Another way of describing this is as two convolutions with kernel size 1.\nThe dimensionality of input and output is dmodel = 512, and the inner-layer has dimensionality\ndff = 2048.\n3.4\nEmbeddings and Softmax\nSimilarly to other sequence transduction models, we use learned embeddings to convert the input\ntokens and output tokens to vectors of dimension dmodel. We also use the usual learned linear transfor-\nmation and softmax function to convert the decoder output to predicted next-token probabilities.	{"type": "text", "page": 5, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"3c93ecef-7507-490f-ae8b-da4f89d6437b\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 5, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"527ca606-4fbd-4701-9897-603afd6015c7\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 5, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"08772a695f0cfd9bcae9d57be0ddaf3e8eca4b01b3acf77b3df02f648b1bef14\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"1a488729-1437-45af-84fa-b05c014875f1\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 5, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"4cc4192bb9cc950e0a250bfb30918c5f411d7426806ed095ab991cac37b88d5e\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"800d91d3-89cd-49b9-a4b6-74b1646d3237\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"43725edcbe87643c9eb201d5ee06bb5f8043f53a2fd76be0dacc4f71c7c9d9b7\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\