86	The positional encodings have the same dimension dmodel\nas the embeddings, so that the two can be summed. There are many choices of positional encodings,\nlearned and ﬁxed [8].\nIn this work, we use sine and cosine functions of different frequencies:\nPE(pos,2i) = sin(pos/100002i/dmodel)\nPE(pos,2i+1) = cos(pos/100002i/dmodel)\nwhere pos is the position and i is the dimension. That is, each dimension of the positional encoding\ncorresponds to a sinusoid. The wavelengths form a geometric progression from 2π to 10000 · 2π.	{"type": "text", "page": 6, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"755416cc-754d-4164-8742-df0efd6a2dc9\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"0f8124c2-0317-4306-859c-c415d4d7cd2e\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"0bf1b0fe9473b0bc07c222551744dd0917f1ac8b87c98fb015c6d220395d8872\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"09e51d2c-9580-40a9-a102-cdc480189fd9\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"bf45ae48d4520d0f80578987f0b3c66e50aeac4699ed8948ca4b629d4fd1bc34\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"b15374b8-e2b0-4d53-a20b-a5d5daeb6d80\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"90ddcca2c48c401be9ddb5b24adc2be06525ad1e8cbdee483fa4f3974ec72188\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\"{key}: {value}\\", \\"metadata_separator\\": \\"\\\\n\\", \\"text\\": \\"\\", \\"mimetype\\": \\"text/plain\\", \\"start_char_idx\\": 565, \\"end_char_idx\\": 1085, \\"text_template\\": \\"{metadata_str}\\\\n\\\\n{content}\\", \\