87	The wavelengths form a geometric progression from 2π to 10000 · 2π. We\nchose this function because we hypothesized it would allow the model to easily learn to attend by\nrelative positions, since for any ﬁxed offset k, PEpos+k can be represented as a linear function of\nPEpos.\nWe also experimented with using learned positional embeddings [8] instead, and found that the two\nversions produced nearly identical results (see Table 3 row (E)). We chose the sinusoidal version\nbecause it may allow the model to extrapolate to sequence lengths longer than the ones encountered\nduring training.	{"type": "text", "page": 6, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"b15374b8-e2b0-4d53-a20b-a5d5daeb6d80\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"0f8124c2-0317-4306-859c-c415d4d7cd2e\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"0bf1b0fe9473b0bc07c222551744dd0917f1ac8b87c98fb015c6d220395d8872\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"755416cc-754d-4164-8742-df0efd6a2dc9\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"6bd5eb7218e7f47a0dc235f0620c791f489e38a9dda5b8a1ee43ff1b15e99ffd\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"6f1729bb-26a7-4125-8002-2939f042e3f6\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"78be928d50a7b217d6780477dd881483adc37e504bc078753454bb95f2e6830d\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\"{key}: {value}\\", \\"metadata_separator\\": \\"\\\\n\\", \\"text\\": \\"\\", \\"mimetype\\": \\"text/plain\\", \\"start_char_idx\\": 1018, \\"end_char_idx\\": 16