90	In terms of\ncomputational complexity, self-attention layers are faster than recurrent layers when the sequence\nlength n is smaller than the representation dimensionality d, which is most often the case with\nsentence representations used by state-of-the-art models in machine translations, such as word-piece\n[31] and byte-pair [25] representations. To improve computational performance for tasks involving\nvery long sequences, self-attention could be restricted to considering only a neighborhood of size r in\n6	{"type": "text", "page": 6, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"62d93e39-74ae-4a8b-bcf0-afc6ebff3054\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"0f8124c2-0317-4306-859c-c415d4d7cd2e\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"0bf1b0fe9473b0bc07c222551744dd0917f1ac8b87c98fb015c6d220395d8872\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"c439b316-dc30-485f-9fc9-6e3771e61414\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 6, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"e7dfb2a7248941538f5359d24e182dfc955fdd89e87da306d8742fea45a02e57\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\"{key}: {value}\\", \\"metadata_separator\\": \\"\\\\n\\", \\"text\\": \\"\\", \\"mimetype\\": \\"text/plain\\", \\"start_char_idx\\": 3033, \\"end_char_idx\\": 3544, \\"text_template\\": \\"{metadata_str}\\\\n\\\\n{content}\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"TextNode\\"}", "_node_type": "TextNode", "document_id": "0f8124c2-0317-4306-859c-c415d4d7cd2e", "doc_id": "0f8124c2-0317-4306-859c-c415d4d7cd2e", "ref_doc_id": "0f8124c2-0317-4306-859c-c415d4d7cd2e"}	62d93e39-74ae-4a8b-bcf0-afc6ebf