95	We varied the learning\nrate over the course of training, according to the formula:\nlrate = d−0.5\nmodel · min(step_num−0.5, step_num · warmup_steps−1.5)\n(3)\nThis corresponds to increasing the learning rate linearly for the ﬁrst warmup_steps training steps,\nand decreasing it thereafter proportionally to the inverse square root of the step number. We used\nwarmup_steps = 4000.\n5.4\nRegularization\nWe employ three types of regularization during training:\nResidual Dropout\nWe apply dropout [27] to the output of each sub-layer, before it is added to the\nsub-layer input and normalized. In addition, we apply dropout to the sums of the embeddings and the\npositional encodings in both the encoder and decoder stacks.	{"type": "text", "page": 7, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"839a08cb-e73e-4827-832f-f32f8e84ad92\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 7, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"0e902346-b83a-4454-9364-885546db8d7c\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 7, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"5c63254d65b0855b33f15154f99ebf6c19fcf9faa76ab3e5228c1da2c24a237b\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"9f7dc3e0-3b2c-4b5e-9008-f7cb681e3ad6\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 7, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"594cdac3c4bea895ae3492cd9b51afa368c55fdcdc60b3d14b946e5de2702388\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"f0f978be-88b4-4b8a-9eb9-2a7aadae073f\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"f82e670dbda66a41e93980254bccde56e3c72ac7910a5585612406cc6ae5f092\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}}, \\"metadata_template\\": \\"{key}: {value}\\", \\"metadata_s