108	For translation tasks, the Transformer can be trained signiﬁcantly faster than architectures based\non recurrent or convolutional layers. On both WMT 2014 English-to-German and WMT 2014\nEnglish-to-French translation tasks, we achieve a new state of the art. In the former task our best\nmodel outperforms even all previously reported ensembles.\nWe are excited about the future of attention-based models and plan to apply them to other tasks. We\nplan to extend the Transformer to problems involving input and output modalities other than text and\nto investigate local, restricted attention mechanisms to efﬁciently handle large inputs and outputs\nsuch as images, audio and video. Making generation less sequential is another research goals of ours.\nThe code we used to train and evaluate our models is available at https://github.com/\ntensorflow/tensor2tensor.	{"type": "text", "page": 9, "source": "attention.pdf", "_node_content": "{\\"id_\\": \\"d4f8bc96-d16c-4a52-b115-76eb03da3ca6\\", \\"embedding\\": null, \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 9, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"excluded_embed_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"excluded_llm_metadata_keys\\": [], \\"relationships\\": {\\"1\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"63f8200b-3029-4c30-860e-efee5a06788c\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"4\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 9, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"b10298b3b4a4b31d47d00b17a66e008824173f6f98b2a43637d312d08051fe18\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"2\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"a22d21d6-32f3-4781-aca9-d961d90b762e\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {\\"type\\": \\"text\\", \\"page\\": 9, \\"source\\": \\"attention.pdf\\"}, \\"hash\\": \\"edfb63f7516b7038eee94893e185279f0ab34a0d4305c78fdc40ef2ca797ed65\\", \\"class_name\\": \\"RelatedNodeInfo\\"}, \\"3\\": {\\"node_id\\": \\"ca9f186f-2db7-4e49-adda-48f2462575a2\\", \\"node_type\\": \\"1\\", \\"metadata\\": {}, \\"hash\\": \\"8e843071979e1d0d2e5847b5d3855